WEBVTT

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:00.096
How funny!

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:04.233
--Is it really that funny?
-I'm sorry.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:07.070
But to think that the brawler
you fought to the death with

00:02:07.094 --> 00:02:09.405
was beaten in one hit...

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:12.642
Hanayama-san wasn't
in his best condition.

00:02:12.666 --> 00:02:17.968
<i>Oh, so he could've beaten
Yujiro Hanma if he had been?</i>

00:02:20.407 --> 00:02:23.920
The little league is
still the little league.

00:02:23.944 --> 00:02:30.008
"Parting Ways"

00:02:36.223 --> 00:02:40.503
Listen. That is what you're aiming for.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:43.573
It shouldn't matter if
the other person is hurt.

00:02:43.597 --> 00:02:47.944
Every challenger must be crushed,
even toddlers.

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:49.595
Fool.

00:02:53.073 --> 00:02:56.099
Here. I'll hold you up.

00:03:09.156 --> 00:03:12.502
He's filled with the pride of
being the world's strongest!

00:03:12.526 --> 00:03:13.789
Am I wrong?

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:22.812
That match was definitely
too gruesome to be called a match.

00:03:22.836 --> 00:03:25.615
We both could've died...

00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:29.439
I've almost died so many times.

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:49.806
--But...
--But...?

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:53.743
| feel a bond between Hanayama-san and me.

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:57.146
I also felt this way when
| sparred with Yuri-san

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.800
and fought the Yasha Ape.

00:04:24.865 --> 00:04:29.812
I've only lived for 13 years,
but I've always looked up to my dad

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.749
and done everything I could possibly do.

00:04:32.773 --> 00:04:34.969
And then I realized something...!

00:04:37.778 --> 00:04:43.192
That my true reason for aiming
to be the strongest is that bond...

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:47.312
And that Dad is completely different!

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:04.227
| have something you'll find interesting.

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:08.375
Here. It's for you.

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:12.043
"To Baki Hanma c/0 Emi Akezawa"

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:15.892
"Kaoru Hanayama"

00:05:15.916 --> 00:05:17.315
"Kaoru Hanayama"
Hanayama-san!

00:05:19.953 --> 00:05:25.255
Such terrible writing. He must've
been too busy fighting to ever study.

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:31.120
"I want to see you."

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:36.501
-- I want to see you.
--Hana-

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:51.809
Hanayama-san...!

00:06:19.179 --> 00:06:20.840
Hanayama-san...!

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:25.695
I really wanted to see ya.

00:06:25.719 --> 00:06:28.689
I tried writing it with my mouth...

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:34.770
--Surprised it even got delivered.
--Hana-

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:38.287
I chose to fight him! I regret nothing!

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:47.631
But I want you to get stronger.

00:06:48.475 --> 00:06:51.035
Even stronger than your old man...

00:06:53.113 --> 00:06:55.480
Even stronger than Dad...!

00:07:02.122 --> 00:07:03.954
You bet I will!

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.557
That's the spirit.

00:07:30.684 --> 00:07:34.678
You need to grow up, Baki.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.448
There's no turning back!

00:08:16.563 --> 00:08:18.554
I will get stronger.

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:29.339
Even stronger than Dad...!

00:08:58.571 --> 00:09:03.519
--Is he playing with a bird?
--No...

00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:07.390
What the young master is
doing is a type of training

00:09:07.414 --> 00:09:11.127
used in Chinese martial arts
to develop the reflexes.

00:09:11.151 --> 00:09:12.461
Seriously?

00:09:12.485 --> 00:09:17.700
When a bird takes flight,
it jumps before flapping its wings.

00:09:17.724 --> 00:09:22.038
By sensing that first jump with
his skin and lowering his arm,

00:09:22.062 --> 00:09:25.760
he's able to prevent the bird
from flapping its wings at all.

00:09:27.934 --> 00:09:31.580
To handle a wild bird in
such a manner, one would need

00:09:31.604 --> 00:09:36.303
exceptional concentration and
reflexes that outclass wild animals.

00:09:39.446 --> 00:09:40.971
Drive.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.568
What the...?

00:10:14.147 --> 00:10:15.615
Dad...

00:10:16.583 --> 00:10:21.885
That's some old training
you're doing there, Sportsman.

00:10:46.279 --> 00:10:49.249
In one month... I will fight you.

00:11:03.429 --> 00:11:07.943
Show me everything you've
learned in 13 years.

00:11:07.967 --> 00:11:11.926
You better make it good. Or else...

00:11:16.142 --> 00:11:21.945
<i>Oh, yes. I have a present for you.
t's not much, but...</i>

00:11:22.715 --> 00:11:26.549
Maybe you'll recognize him!

00:11:27.053 --> 00:11:28.452
It can't be...!

00:11:32.725 --> 00:11:36.705
The Yasha Ape!

00:11:36.729 --> 00:11:38.754
Show's over!

00:11:44.137 --> 00:11:48.165
| can't believe this chimp
gave you a hard time!

00:12:01.888 --> 00:12:04.414
Yujiro!

00:12:05.425 --> 00:12:08.087
Yujiro!

00:12:26.746 --> 00:12:29.044
Yujiro!

00:12:52.472 --> 00:12:54.406
Yasha. ...I

00:13:08.254 --> 00:13:10.532
How dare you...

00:13:10.556 --> 00:13:13.002
How dare you do this...!

00:13:13.026 --> 00:13:15.738
Yes! That's the look!

00:13:15.762 --> 00:13:19.508
You can't let someone this
terrible get off scott free!

00:13:19.532 --> 00:13:21.694
Even if that person is your father!

00:13:23.303 --> 00:13:29.640
Listen! People this horrible
absolutely must pay!

00:13:43.489 --> 00:13:45.467
Baki...

00:13:45.491 --> 00:13:47.550
One month...!

00:13:56.536 --> 00:13:58.834
Get away!

00:14:31.871 --> 00:14:33.669
Yasha...

00:14:42.782 --> 00:14:44.944
Your wife.

00:14:47.487 --> 00:14:52.425
Six years ago, my father
took this from you.

00:15:14.347 --> 00:15:19.261
Thanks to you, I've grown stronger!

00:15:19.285 --> 00:15:21.219
Thank you very much!

00:15:30.163 --> 00:15:31.756
A fang...

00:16:06.933 --> 00:16:09.834
1'tl beat him!

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:18.807
Baki.

00:16:25.117 --> 00:16:29.315
How long has it been?
You've really grown.

00:16:34.827 --> 00:16:40.742
- I hear you're fighting Yujiro.
--Strydom-san! Where is he?!

00:16:40.766 --> 00:16:44.279
Not so fast. You still have a month.

00:16:44.303 --> 00:16:49.798
Fighting Yujiro now would be
like a rabbit fighting a lion.

00:16:50.643 --> 00:16:54.477
I'll beat him! I'll get
stronger than him!

00:17:01.754 --> 00:17:04.348
Then there's only one way.

00:17:05.591 --> 00:17:13.021
The very source of Yujiro's strength...
is his ego.

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:22.100
He fiercely believes that nothing
can ever be as strong as him.

00:17:23.876 --> 00:17:30.179
<i>Many "great fighters” have
fallen to his tenacious spirit.</i>

00:17:31.884 --> 00:17:35.184
"I am the strongest! I am the greatest!”

00:17:36.556 --> 00:17:44.122
The last place that a man goes to
get such an ego is the battlefield.

00:17:44.897 --> 00:17:48.143
The Middle East,
Africa, eastern Europe...

00:17:48.167 --> 00:17:50.312
...and the most dangerous place of all.

00:17:50.336 --> 00:17:53.615
It was there that Yujiro's ego
acquired the greatest satisfaction.

00:17:53.639 --> 00:17:58.787
It was there that Yujiro's
fighting techniques fully blossomed.

00:17:58.811 --> 00:18:02.941
I know because I saw his
horridness with my own eyes.

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:10.822
Captain Strydom. I want you
to show me to this place.

00:18:11.724 --> 00:18:14.091
You're sure of this?

00:18:31.711 --> 00:18:34.156
Go to Hokkaido.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:36.258
Hokkaido...?

00:18:36.282 --> 00:18:39.461
There you will find your battlefield.

00:18:39.485 --> 00:18:44.685
A scene of carnage that would easily
rival Yujiro's own battlefields.

00:18:47.393 --> 00:18:52.407
<i>"Hokkaido"</i>

00:18:52.431 --> 00:18:53.830
General!

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:06.838
What happened, Division Commander?

00:19:09.448 --> 00:19:11.760
| asked you a question!

00:19:11.784 --> 00:19:17.746
I'm sorry to report that
they've decimated Unit 001!

00:19:19.392 --> 00:19:24.072
Defeated by a unit of
only five unarmed men?!

00:19:24.096 --> 00:19:26.308
Pathetic!

00:19:26.332 --> 00:19:29.411
You don't understand, General!

00:19:29.435 --> 00:19:32.314
If we can hear the enemy,
we can get near them!

00:19:32.338 --> 00:19:35.384
If we can see the enemy,
we can die honorable deaths!

00:19:35.408 --> 00:19:40.155
But what can we do if
they're silent and unseen?!

00:19:40.179 --> 00:19:42.691
Unseen?!

00:19:42.715 --> 00:19:46.862
My unit still hasn't sighted them!

00:19:46.886 --> 00:19:51.867
We only know they're out
there when they attack us!

00:19:51.891 --> 00:19:53.620
What?!

00:20:02.368 --> 00:20:05.847
There is a professional militant group
that seeks the smell of blood,

00:20:05.871 --> 00:20:10.318
belongs to no one,
and loves blood more than money.

00:20:10.342 --> 00:20:16.281
There's only 5 of them, but they're
stronger than an entire regiment.

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:21.463
A few days ago, the Self Defense Force
invited them to Hokkaido

00:20:21.487 --> 00:20:25.801
as a practice enemy, but training
and war are the same to them.

00:20:25.825 --> 00:20:28.737
The SDF was crushed in no time.

00:20:28.761 --> 00:20:32.959
Right about now, they're probably
roughing it in the primeval forest.

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:38.733
Every place they go
transforms into a battlefield.

00:20:43.075 --> 00:20:45.787
If only we knew their location...

00:20:45.811 --> 00:20:50.339
I'm sorry, General!
It doesn't make sense!

00:20:51.984 --> 00:20:54.763
Can we really call this training?!

00:20:54.787 --> 00:20:59.434
We didn't intend to train
against enemies like that!

00:20:59.458 --> 00:21:03.939
Division Commander.
They're making a statement.

00:21:03.963 --> 00:21:07.642
That without casualties, they can
injure however many they want...

00:21:07.666 --> 00:21:11.113
That they can destroy
however many tanks they want...

00:21:11.137 --> 00:21:13.782
In other words, this is no exercise!

00:21:13.806 --> 00:21:15.865
It's a war between us and them!

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:21.656
Some people even call them warmongers.

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:25.794
But that is precisely what you need now.

00:21:25.818 --> 00:21:28.048
This is a war with Yujiro!

00:21:29.054 --> 00:21:32.667
Losing in a war against them means death.

00:21:32.691 --> 00:21:35.683
Do you still want to go Hokkaido?

00:22:46.165 --> 00:22:51.713
The hazy afternoon in the winter sun

00:22:51.737 --> 00:22:57.319
hangs onto love in one
corner of the pavement

00:22:57.343 --> 00:23:02.991
When I blew on my cold hands

00:23:03.015 --> 00:23:07.996
a tiny bit of courage swelled up.

00:23:08.020 --> 00:23:13.535
Today will certainly be wonderful,

00:23:13.559 --> 00:23:19.074
gently enveloped in love

00:23:19.098 --> 00:23:24.746
There are some strange feelings too,

00:23:24.770 --> 00:23:30.285
but they will be reborn

00:23:30.309 --> 00:23:35.957
Today will certainly be wonderful;

00:23:35.981 --> 00:23:42.580
they will be reborn as even more love.

00:23:51.330 --> 00:23:53.196
"Next Episode”

00:23:55.467 --> 00:23:58.280
The game of war has begun.

00:23:58.304 --> 00:24:03.685
The five hunters are silent,
imperceptible, and elusive.

00:24:03.709 --> 00:24:07.455
He remembers that killing
is the origin of fighting.

00:24:07.479 --> 00:24:13.228
But there's one other person:
the lord of massacre.

00:24:13.252 --> 00:24:16.197
Soon, he will awaken.

00:24:16.221 --> 00:24:21.057
"Next Episode: Battlefield”
